course: dictionary
lesson: 1890
title: Meet the colobus
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words name animals you may never have seen. You can often work out what they are from the words around them. «Chimpanzees eat mostly fruit but sometimes hunt monkeys like the colobus as a team.» The word like puts the colobus beside monkeys, so a colobus must be a kind of monkey.
explain: A colobus is a slender African monkey with long silky fur and a long tail. It lives high in forest trees and eats mostly leaves. Its thumb is only a stump, but it can still leap between branches.
explain: The best-known colobus is black and white, but there are others, such as the red colobus. "Colobus monkey" is another name for the same animal, so you can use either phrase.
fact: A colobus is a slender African monkey with long silky fur.
fact: A colobus has a long tail and only a stump instead of a thumb.
fact: The best-known colobus is black and white.
fact: Colobus monkeys live high in forest trees and eat mostly leaves.
fact: Colobus monkeys have a special stomach with many parts, which helps them digest tough leaves.
exercise: «Chimpanzees eat mostly fruit but sometimes hunt monkeys like the colobus as a team.» What kind of animal is a colobus? | A snake | *A monkey | A bird | A fish
exercise: A colobus has a long tail and silky fur. Where does it usually live? | On the ground in the desert | In a cave | Under the sea | *High in forest trees
exercise: Which part of a colobus is only a stump? | Its tail | *Its thumb | Its nose | Its fur
test: What does a colobus mostly eat? | Insects | Fruit | Meat | *Leaves
test: Which colour is the best-known colobus? | *Black and white | Brown and grey | Red and blue | Green and yellow
exam: Which sentence describes a colobus correctly? | A slow reptile that lives in rivers | *A slender African monkey with long silky fur | A small fish with fins | A large bird that flies over the sea
